ballparking is a technique that helps us  to solve problems quickly instead of  trying to get a perfect result we make a  fast intelligent guess just like in  baseball to score we don't need to hit  the ball perfectly often we just need to  keep it inside the ballpark the  technique is useful in conversations and  is essential to passing certain tests to  watch this video most effectively grab a  pen and paper and try solving the  following two problems as we present  them just pause whenever you see this  sign  let's start easy what do you think is  the most popular food in the world could  it be Italian Japanese American fast  food or something else as it is  impossible to get an exact answer let's  look at what we maybe already know in  Italy there are around 50 million people  in Japan about a hundred million and in  North America about 500 million but in  China or in India that lives over a  billion people now we can use the  process of elimination and make a  ballpark estimate that Chinese and  Indian food is probably the most popular  try something a little harder imagine  that you were doing a complicated maths  test for something like the GMAT exam  then you might have just two minutes to  solve complex problems in your head  maybe something like the square root of  five times the square root of 24 plus  five divided by five plus two times the  square root of six then you're given  five multiple-choice answers  a B C D or E if we would try to solve it  we will probably run out of time  ballparking is now the only option you  can try it on your own  or do it with us  look at the equation let's look at the  first part the square root of 24 since  the square root of 24 is difficult to  calculate in your head think of a close  enough number to the square root of 24  that will be easier for you the square  root of 25 comes to mind to which the  answer is 5 let's now write down the new  simpler equation and then again even  simpler now what about the fraction it  looks hard but let's try  even if we don't know what five plus two  times the square root of six is we do  know that it's more than five so let's  write it again and just call the  denominator more than five and because 5  divided by anything larger than five  must be smaller than one let's write 25  plus less than one or the square root of  25 and that equals approximately five  let's now look at the options we were  given  look at the equation and each possible  choice  a is clear and doesn't look bad B is  five plus two times the square root of  six which is something like seven or  more that doesn't look right C is the  square root of something that comes out  to be three or less that's too small  what about D the square root of 120 we  don't know that but we do know that the  square root of a hundred is ten let's  just write ten or more that looks too  high last there is e five divided by two  times the square root of six now for two  times the square root of six let's just  write more than two and five divided by  something that's more than two also  looks too small now we can use the  process of elimination and cross out all  the wrong answers to see what's left a  it is  now it's your turn tribal barking the  amount of views that you think this  video will have by the end of this year  and when your favorite sprouts gift on  patreon.com slash sprouts we will count  all entries submitted by August the 31st  and announce the winner on the 1st of  January to join just leave your ballpark  figure in the comments below and if you  want tell us how you did it those of you  who post later than August the 31st will  enter next year's round of sprouts  ballpark Awards good luck  you
 

